	Gurus,

I had asked:

> I am running 4.0f with Enhanced Security and cde as my login manager.  =
The
> security people here are requiring me to disable XDMCP.  Here is what =
I have
> tried so far
[snip]
>   2. Adding the entry to /usr/var/X11/xdm/Xaccess:
> !*
>=20
> How can I eliminate any vestige of an XDMCP server?

Thanks to Trevor Osatchuk, Michael Polnick and Eric Sisson who asked =
about the files in /etc/dt/config/.  I didn't have a /etc/dt/config =
directory.  Once I created it and copied over the modified files Xaccess =
and Xconfig, all is well.  Eric also pointed out that this is documented =
in dtlogin(1).

Thanks to all.  This is a great list.

                          --Harvey Rarback



